{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ghost-playback-011-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/WatchModeControllerTests.cs","line":234,"method":"ProcessWatchEndHoldTimer_DebrisOnlyChild_DoesNotAutoFollowDuringHold","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/WatchModeController.cs:2565; drop the gs.ghost==null deferral in TransferWatchToNextSegment so a ghost-less state transfers -> red","what_it_asserts":"After ProcessWatchEndHoldTimer runs with a debris-only child branch, handled=true, watchedRecordingIndex stays 0, hold deadline stays float.MaxValue and both ghost states survive.","why_weak":"engine.ghostStates[1] is constructed with ghost==null, so TransferWatchToNextSegment returns false on the deferral guard regardless of what FindNextWatchTarget picks. If the debris exclusion in GhostPlaybackLogic.FindNextWatchTarget were removed the test would still be green.","proposed_action":"Assert directly that controller.FindNextWatchTarget(0, root) == -1, or give ghostStates[1] a non-null ghost stand-in so the transfer path is reachable and a wrong target actually moves watchedRecordingIndex.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ghost-playback-011-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/WatchModeControllerTests.cs","line":1021,"method":"CanRestoreMapFocus_MissingMapObject_StaysDeferred","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/WatchModeController.Diagnostics.cs:160; invert the comparison to != \"ready\" -> red","what_it_asserts":"CanRestoreMapFocus returns false when hasMapObject is false.","why_weak":"Only the negative arm is pinned and no other test calls CanRestoreMapFocus, so a body reduced to return false keeps the suite green while map-focus restore would never fire.","proposed_action":"Add the ready-case assertion (all four inputs satisfied -> true) next to the existing negative case.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ghost-playback-011-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/WatchModeControllerTests.cs","line":1202,"method":"ShouldIgnoreOverlapCycleEvent_ReadyForNextSentinel_IgnoresRealEvent","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/WatchModeController.Runtime.cs:152; change != to == -> both red","what_it_asserts":"Sentinel watched-cycle values (-1 ready-for-next, -2 holding) cause a real overlap cycle event to be ignored.","why_weak":"The SUT is one expression, eventCycleIndex != watchedCycleIndex. The two sentinel facts and ShouldIgnoreOverlapCycleEvent_NonWatchedCycle_Ignored assert the same branch and the same observable with different data rows.","proposed_action":"Collapse the three true-arm facts into one [Theory] with InlineData rows (3,5), (7,-1), (4,-2), keeping the false-arm fact separate.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ghost-playback-011-04","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/WatchModeControllerTests.cs","line":806,"method":"CompensateTransferredWatchAngles_RawWorldDirectionStateProjectsOntoNewTargetBasis","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"medium","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/WatchModeController.cs:1352; break DecomposeOrbitDirectionInTargetFrame -> both red","what_it_asserts":"The HasWorldOrbitDirection branch of CompensateTransferredWatchAngles preserves the world orbit direction within a 0.999 cosine.","why_weak":"CompensateTransferredWatchAngles_WorldOrbitDirection_PreservesDirection already pins that branch with the identical round-trip assertion; only the input vectors and angles differ. The same applies to the ChainTransferBoundary fact versus TargetRelativeStateIgnoresNewTargetRotation.","proposed_action":"Merge each pair into one [Theory] with the two data rows, keeping the bug-history comments on the theory.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
